                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is a healthy D2C contribution margin?</h3>
                                        <p>20-40% depending on category. Below 15% typically indicates model risk. Above 40% is exceptional.</p>
                                        <h3>How long before I know my LTV?</h3>
                                        <p>12-month LTV needs 12+ months of cohort data. Early estimates carry high uncertainty.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest D2C financial model mistake?</h3>
                                        <p>Ignoring returns cost + working capital + COGS creep. All three erode margin invisibly.</p>
                                        <h3>Should I optimise for MER or contribution margin?</h3>
                                        <p>Contribution margin. MER can hide unit economic problems + misalign with actual profitability.</p>
